        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-30T12:30:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this means you can never read the clipboard if writeClipboardToVm never succeeds. And you can never write to the clipboard if readClipboardFromVm never succeeds.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 781,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 781,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "a9d7283ffd7a1a8335abfafab85a5814bcf99806",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18e4aa85_4477985b",
        "filename": "android/VmLauncherApp/java/com/android/virtualization/vmlauncher/MainActivity.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 781,
      "author": {
        "id": 1950816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-07-31T02:00:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s intended. Succeeding here means clipboard things worked well as intended, not actual clipboard contents are modified for the update. So returning false from `writeClipboardToVm` or `readClipboardFromVm` represents there was an error.\n\nIf there\u0027s an error from any side, vice versa wouldn\u0027t work.",
      "parentUuid": "e4c41d9e_72400f3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 781,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 781,
        "endChar": 42
      },
      "revId": "a9d7283ffd7a1a8335abfafab85a5814bcf99806",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "37ec7f13_0c881cb7",
        "filename": "android/VmLauncherApp/java/com/android/virtualization/vmlauncher/MainActivity.java",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 781,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T10:53:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No. Failing to read from clipboard doesn\u0027t necessarily mean that you shouldn\u0027t be able to write to clipboard (and vice versa).\n\nIn general, you shouldn\u0027t have a loop that can possibly run forever in a message handler because that loop can prevent other messages from being handled.",
      "parentUuid": "18e4aa85_4477985b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 781,
        "startChar": 36,
        "endLine": 781,
